        "committer": {
          "name": "Oleg Drokin",
          "email": "green@whamcloud.com",
          "date": "2026-08-22 03:26:32.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-20561 tests: fix lock count retrieval in sanity-flr",
        "message": "LU-20561 tests: fix lock count retrieval in sanity-flr\n\nget_osc_lock_count() matched client OSC namespaces using\nldlm.namespaces.-OST%04x-osc-[-0-9a-f]*.lock_count.\n\nWhen a second client is mounted, another -OST%04x-osc- namespace\nis created, so get_param returns one lock_count value per line.\n\nAssigning this multi-line output to count causes\nlock_count=$((lock_count + count)) to fail with an arithmetic\nsyntax error. As a result, in $(get_osc_lock_count ...), the\nsubshell exits before reaching echo, leaving the command\nsubstitution empty. This causes test_22/test_31 to fail with\n\"unary operator expected\" and \"glimpse requests were sent\".\n\nUse total_used_locks() to sum the lock counts from all matching\nnamespaces. Pass ...-osc-[-0-9a-f] so the helper's *...* pattern\nstill matches client hex instance IDs while excluding OSP\nnamespaces such as ...-osc-MDT*.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity-flr env=MOUNT_2=yes,ONLY=22+31\nTest-Parameters: clientdistro=ubuntu2604 testlist=sanity-flr env=MOUNT_2=yes,ONLY=22+31\nFixes: 526dbd3d8723 (\"LU-9771 flr: read support for flr\")\nSigned-off-by: Chakshu Kansal <ckansal@ddn.com>\nChange-Id: Ic35b4db13eeb0a64f70e9929603c6c9723ae6bf5\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/67809\nReviewed-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Jian Yu <yujian@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
